course: dictionary
lesson: 9274
title: Spacious: big and roomy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Spacious means big and roomy. A spacious room has a lot of space inside it. Context helps you check this: «The kids loved their spacious garden, with room to run and kick a ball.» Room to run tells you the garden is big.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Swap in big. A big room is a spacious room, so the meaning fits. In writing, spacious can be better than big for a room, because it tells the reader about the space inside.
explain: Watch out for the phrase «deceptively spacious». Deceptively means it looks like something it is not. In UK house adverts, «deceptively spacious» often means the home is smaller than it seems. Compact also means small, so read the whole advert carefully.
fact: Spacious means big and roomy, with a lot of space inside.
fact: «A spacious kitchen» is a kitchen with plenty of room to move around.
fact: Spacious is often a better word than big when you describe a room, a house or a car.
fact: In maths, area tells you how spacious a room is: length × width.
fact: «Deceptively spacious» in a UK house advert often means the home is small. Compact also means small.
exercise: «The family moved into a spacious house with a big garden.» What does spacious mean? | Noisy and busy | Dark and cold | *Big and roomy | Old and falling down
exercise: Which word would you use to describe a room with lots of space inside, instead of big? | Glum | *Spacious | Compact | Curt
exercise: In maths, how do you find the area that tells you how spacious a room is? | Number of windows | Length + width | *Length × width | Height ÷ 2
test: An estate agent says «deceptively spacious» about a flat. What does this usually suggest? | The flat is huge and empty | The flat has no windows | The flat is the best in town | *The flat is smaller than it looks
test: Which word is a better choice than big for a room with lots of space? | Gloomy | Compact | Tiny | *Spacious
exam: Mia writes «The hall was spacious, with room for twenty chairs and a long table.» Why is spacious a good choice here? | Because it is a colour | *Because it tells the reader about the roomy space inside | Because it means very old | Because it means small
